## 11. Error Handling Matrix

| Failure Scenario | Behavior | Impact |
|------------------|----------|--------|
| L1 miss | Normal, proceed to L2 | None |
| L2 read timeout | Log error, skip L2, call origin for all L1 misses | Slightly slower, but functional |
| L2 cluster down | Same as timeout | Same |
| L2 deserialization error (corrupt data) | Log warning, treat that entry as miss | Re-fetched from origin |
| L2 write failure | Log warning, continue | Entry will be re-fetched next time |
| Origin (Proxy API) failure | Exception propagates to caller | Real failure, handled by existing error handling |

**The golden rule: cache failures never prevent the indexing pipeline from functioning.**

